 "release": 0.5,
 "sustained": false,
 "gain": 1.0,
 "notes": "Yamaha C5, AB stereo pair. 30 notes A0-C8 sampled every minor third, two velocity layers: vel 48 = Salamander layer v6 (soft, darker), vel 96 = layer v12 (medium-loud). Both layers are loudness-matched to each other and across the range, so the engine should apply its own velocity gain and use the layer only for timbre (suggested split at velocity ~72, or crossfade 56-88). Per-note tuning corrections from the Retuned SFZ shipped with V3 were applied. Natural decay, trimmed to 6 s (bass) .. 2 s (top octave) with a fade; for longer held notes let the release envelope take over. Same samples work for bright_acoustic_piano with a high-shelf boost. Recommended release 0.4-0.6 s (dampers)."
}
